    "Description": "A transparency slide showing the top of the head of a carousel pig. The pig is very well worn. The skin is light tan at the top and fades to a darker brown towards the bottom of the pig. The saddle can be seen at the bottom of the image and is brown. The tack is red. The ears area different shade of brown, suggesting that they have been recently replaced. The pig is on a pole, which is coming up through the pig at the front of the saddle. The slide reads “PULLEN PARK CAROUSEL PULLEN PARK 16B top head” at the top and “RALEIGH WAKE CO S.S. 8.5.81” at the bottom. Stamped up the side is “JUL81D9”.",
